        "snippet": "Assessing Virgin Galactic (SPCE) Valuation After Q1 2026 Results And New US$40.21m Shelf Registration - Simply Wall St News\n\nAdvertisement\n\nVirgin Galactic Holdings (SPCE) is back in focus after its first quarter 2026 results and a fresh US$40.21 million shelf registration. This combination spotlights both funding plans and the path toward commercial flights.\n\nSee our latest analysis for Virgin Galactic Holdings.\n\nThe stock’s recent moves reflect that tension, with the share price down 14.59% year to date but showing a 9.77% 90 day share price return, while the 1 year total shareholder return declined 41.46%. This points to fading long term momentum despite short term interest around earnings and the new shelf registration.\n\nIf Virgin Galactic’s story has you thinking about where else early stage ideas might emerge, this is a good moment to scan 26 quantum computing stocks\n\nWith Q1 results showing smaller losses, a fresh US$40.21 million shelf in place, and the stock trading well below",
